  "companyID": "58c62e995865713647a7115d",
  "created": "2021-05-21T03:42:12.209Z",
  "deletedAt": null,
  "details": "Currently network IDs for objects are determined based on their position in the hierarchy. This makes it difficult to make PC/Quest cross-compatible worlds (eg, you can't just EditorOnly out a whole tree of PC-specific stuff), and makes it so the smallest changes to a world break instances with mixed versions.\nThis could be avoided if network IDs were statically assigned based on a metadata component attached to network-relevant game objects. This could be attached by the SDK as a hidden component to objects missing IDs during the build process (ideally, to EditorOnly objects as well to help with the PC/Quest use case).",
